INSERT INTO `seeding` (`id`, `location`, `eventdate`, `compid`, `createdate`, `writeup`, `googlemap`, `starttime`, `endtime`, `www`, `address`) VALUES
(1, 'Royal Brighton', '2013-02-08', 1, '2013-08-11 13:07:23', 'After a week of 30+ temperatures, a subtle cool change came through making for perfect conditions in the Barnbougle Seeding event.\r\n\r\nRoyal Brighton was in tip-top nick and presented all with an opportunity to establish some form coming into the 3 day event in Tassie in 4 weeks time.\r\n\r\nThe Purple Headed Warrior dropped a massive bombshell to commence proceedings, enlightening the team that there are no motorised carts on the tour, after the initial shock I think we can all agree we just need to man up - sacrifices must be made to get the opportunity to play on Australia`s best public course and one of the worlds top 100!\r\n\r\nPussy Forrest was in scintillating form, ever consistent off the tee showing he`ll be a force to be reckoned with in Van Demons Land. With a few more cheeky nines under his belt allowing a little more touch around the greens he should be fairly well placed in a months time.\r\n\r\nThe day however belonged to Purple, leaving the ego at home and concentrating on a good tempo and consistent approach he absolutely blitzed the course shooting a 20 over par 87, those queries pundits had over his mental toughness and ability to play 18 holes seem to have been put to bed.\r\n\r\nThe Smoking Dolphin also showed some ripping form, his long game was back on song with some huge drives. With a 48 in and out he had no real shocking blow outs, and left a couple out there... a few more games under the belt prior to the main event will blow off any remaining cobwebs and put him well in contention.\r\n\r\nBig Daddy Richo aka Johnny Blue had an interesting day on the course, ending the day with a solid 96 -  at his best he was chipping in for birdie, but hit 2 trees on the first and lost two balls on the 10th so it`s hard to gauge exactly where he`s at. The gap between his best and worst will need to narrow if he`s to perform well on the map of taz.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
(2, 'Royal Sandringham', '2013-02-17', 1, '2013-08-14 22:14:01', 'Well, the heat was cranked up for the second and final Barnbougle seeding round, both literally and metaphorically.\r\n\r\nWith temperatures well into their 30`s all week it was a warm one, however the grounds keeper had obviously turned the sprinklers on last night and then had a few shandy`s because the course was sodden, making for some challenging conditions.\r\n\r\nPussy graced us with his presence for a full 18 holes thus continuing his grand master plan of preparation and training for the big event. He came ready to rumble, pulling out some massive sledges as early as hole number 5 and not letting up until late into the round. He had a mixed bag as far as they days play went. Some glorious tee shots to which we have come accustomed, but also some forgettable off fairway play. One thing he can take out of today is his sand play which improved dramatically as the day went on.\r\n\r\nMole Raper aka Johnny Blue aka Big Daddy Richo continued his form of acquiring a new nickname every round. But it was the gift from the Cheese and Kisses which stole the show, with Moley pulling out the new driver on the first tee and never looking back. A blistering 6 over from the first 10 holes showed us what he is capable of, however he started to crumble around the 13th and never quite got his rhythm back. Some vocal pundits were quick to call that maybe he is peaking a little too early.\r\n\r\nThe Smoking Dolphin kept puffing away and turned in a very similar round to last week. His tee shots and putting were a sight to behold - especially after some sledges from the the Forrest. However his shots around the green and bunker play showed that he`s still lacking that touch required to get the scores down to where he is a capable of. The short game comes with practice so a few more outings prior to the Map of Tas should see him hitting form at the right time. \r\n\r\nPurple had an interesting day on the course, connecting well with his long game the radar seemed a little off, but no one could argue that he wasn`t hitting them cleanly. Ever crisp whether off the tee or from the ground, Purple showed us that whilst off-road golf may be extreme and fun, it tends to have an undesirable effect on the scorecard - playing from the trees more often was the only discernible difference between this week and last. Once he gets his alignment right there won`t be much stopping him.\r\n\r\n\r\nIt will be interesting to see what the Purple Headed Worrier does with the handicaps. Once the official handicaps have been published, Moley and the Dolphin will work on the player review and get the official tournament odds courtesy of Sportsbet, that is of course unless Purple doesn`t give us our handicaps until we`re teeing off in Tasmania - if that`s the case there will be no player review.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
(9, 'Sandringham', '2014-01-19', 2, '2013-10-13 09:05:46', 'After the fun a frivolity of the festive season there was some disorganisation which threatened seeding event 3, but Rimmer came through and sorted what turned out to be a cracking round of golf for 5 of the tours faithful.\r\n\r\nThe confusion crept into the days play with Pussy arriving at the Markers house only to find he was already on course and didn`t need a lift, however once that little faux pas was out the way we could all get down to some solid golfing!\r\n\r\n3 representatives were afflicted by injury; \r\n- Rimmer broke his toe kicking a piece of furniture in anger after a bad round the week before.\r\n- The Marker, so excited to be part of the tour sprained his ankle whilst jumping for joy, but was still able to make it out on course.\r\n- Pussy, well what wasn`t wrong with Pussy? Gout in the knee, tennis elbow, and shaggers back all impeded his play, but he soldiered on.\r\n \r\nAs one of only 2 fit people for the round, Moley got off to a flyer securing 26 points on the front nine with some dashing drives and solid all round play earning him 2 pars and a birdie off the stick. \r\n\r\nHungry showed his appetite for the game by playing a practice round the day before and hitting the range prior to the seeding round which paid dividends with him bringing home the chocolates scoring a whopping 46 points. Competitors could learn a lot from his wise use of the power play, which scored him an extra 7 points for the day.  There is no doubt Hungry is taking the training seriously and is 100% focused on lifting the Shankers trophy. But has he peaked too soon?\r\n\r\nRimmer thought he was out of touch once again with a few scratchings on the front nine, but after Moley tallied his score at the half way mark he was found to have amassed 21 points already and finished on an impressive 36. Signs of the old Rimmers sweet drive down the line were enough evidence that hell be timing his return to form just right.\r\n\r\nThe Marker hadn`t swung a golf club for a while, but you could see the class shining through at points, although a little bit rusty he managed 30 points and will be a force on tour with a few more games under his belt. He showed some good stroke play and was unlucky with the putting, with a fair few rimmers, including a dubious drop in after 10 secs teetering on the edge.  The Markers weakness is definitely the back nine, with a notable drop in standards, so stamina could be an issue during the tournament. However better use of the powerplay should see the Marker near the top of the leaderboard on the day. \r\n\r\nPussy had another round to forget, but given his list of ailments we can`t take that as a reflection of form. We`re all aware that after disastrous seeding coming into the Smitty Invitational in 2013 he took out the competition... it will be interesting to see whether his strategy works this time around with a fairer handicapping system in place. Some glimmer of hope as his ball finding skills in the bushes were easily the strongest part of his game - this could save a few strokes in the Barnbougle love grass.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
(10, 'St Andrews Beach', '2014-03-02', 2, '2013-10-13 09:06:09', 'The last seeding event before the championship and there was a lot to play for with handicaps being a carefully guarded secret amongst tournament organisers. Further to this rumours were abound of bonuses and penalties to even up the field which lead to an anxious group making its way down to the Mornington Peninsula.\r\n\r\nSt Andrews certainly lived up to its eclectic reputation and the Melbourne weather, although chilly to start, turned it on for those who ventured down the highway. The Moth was again a noticeable absentee preferring to brave the tournament organisers rathe. Purple was a confirmed no starter for the tournament and although not here for the day of play he would be happy to know that the banter started early.\r\n\r\nThe attendees split into 2 groups with Hungry, Marker and Pussy leading the charge. In typical fashion Hungry lead the way with a crisp clean iron drive to the middle of the fairway. Marker not to be outdone referred to his trusty GPS caddy which advised him that the driver was best of the tee. Not known for confrontation he begrudgingly accepted the advice and was rewarded with another Marker stonker down the middle of the fairway setting up an easy 2 on. Pussy on the other hand had nowhere to hide on the windswept links course and precisely found the love grass which ended up delaying the start of the second group. While the author was in the second group, the aforementioned review of group 1 would remain fairly precise for the remainder of the day.\r\n\r\nGroup 2 saw the familiar characters of Rimmer, Moley and Dolph paired yet again and while the waiting for Pussy to find his balls was distracting the focus of this group was unquestionable with 3 solid hits of the tee.\r\n\r\nGroup 2 faced the familiar peaks and troughs not dissimilar to the ocean waves enveloping the course. Rimmer was mostly solid of the tee with the mid game ebb and flowing as the carts zoomed around the front 9. Moley was finding some extremely impressive form and had some extremely unlucky chips on the green to not find the bottom of the cup. Dolph was just happy to be out of the office and under the haze of a very unusual fog, unprecedented for this time of year or even in this location, he meandered his way alongside Rimmer as forthcoming holidays and fast cars were discussed.\r\n\r\nBy the turn, Group 2 were tightly bunched and the daily prize was jokingly discussed which by the end of the day was not going to see the calloused hands of any of the group 2 members. Rimmer belted and bashed his way through the back 9 to end up on a very respectable 34. Dolph had his familiar back 9 faded out which undid much of his hard work on the front 9. Moley only got better as the day went on to end up on 41 which for all intents and purposes looked like a day high score.\r\n\r\nGroup 1 finally made their way back to the clubhouse and with the praises of Marker being sonneted by Pussy one would have thought hed actually done enough to overthrow the Seeding event champion in Hungry. But Hungry showed why he would clearly be one of the favourites going into Tasmania finished on an unbelievable 53 to take home the daily prize. A few frothies and stories prior to the long drive home instilled the camaraderie and before we knew it another seeding event was over.\r\n\r\nWould Hungry carry the form thats seen him destroy all comers into Tasmania? Does the Moth really exist and will his reputation (real or not) see him challenge? Was Pussy faking so that we wouldnt be penalised come tournament time? Questions that only time will answer. Until Tasmania, this is Dolphin....out!', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
(7, 'The Dunes', '2013-10-20', 2, '2013-09-13 09:42:08', 'The first seeding event of the Shankers saw a committed and energetic group of 6 make their way down to the Mornington Peninsula for what promised to be a day off great golf, weather, camaraderie and jovial banter. The Moth was an early absentee due to prior sponsorship commitments whilst Glee Balls was a late withdrawal due to a logistical issue.\r\n\r\nAs is Shankers tradition, the first pairing on the tee saw last year`s winner Pussy paired up with Hungry and the subsequent tee shots would set the tone of how the day was to unfold with Hungry finding the middle of the fairway and Pussy (in typical tanking fashion) skewing his drive to the right.The second group of Rim job, Moley, Purple and the dolphin waited arduously while Pussy meandered his way through the thicket in search of his ball (that`s what she said) and this resulted in mixed drives from the second group with only Moley holding any claim of a solid drive.\r\n\r\nThe first 9 for the second grouping saw more lows than high`s with minimal Stableford points taken except for Moley who continued to steadily rack up points in the bank although some questionable points scoring on the first 2 holes was rectified down on the 3rd after the points committee had concluded that he was scoring for the wrong holes.\r\n\r\nRim job and dolphin drove and puffed their way around and from the 4th hole onwards started building up the points while Purple was desperately unlucky with some horrible lies and dropped shots which was a sign to come from him for the remainder of the day. Bad golf it wasn`t, unlucky golf it was.\r\n\r\nBy the turn the Hungry had a comfortable lead over Rim job, Moley and Dolphin with Purple and Pussy languishing at the tail. A quick changeover of groups was suggested and Hungry, Pussy and the puffing brothers paired up to bring the seeding event home. The Course marshals were a constant sight on the back 9 which added more pressure to the usually unflappable Pussy and in typical English fashion he didn`t trouble or challenge the leader-board for the remainder of the day.\r\n\r\nHungry consistently racked up the points and showed why he is the early favourite to take out the event in March. Rim job and Dolphin we`re going at it neck and neck with the PowerPlay holes the only saving grace for Dolphin. At the last we saw an incredible chip on the green from Moley who showed why his short game will keep in the hunt in Tasmania.\r\n\r\nIn the end it was Hungry`s consistency that saw him take out the seeding event winning with a score of 38 while Rim Job, 35 and Dolphin 34 kept him honest but were too inconsistent to mount an real challenge. Moley solidified 4th spot with a score of 28 and Pussy, 18 and Purple, 17 rounded out the leader board. Tanking has been raised as a concern and the tournament committee will be reviewing this event and subsequent seeding events to ensure that the game is not being bought into disrepute.\r\n\r\nThe next seeding event should be a much closer affair with Waterford Valley not expect to present the challenges faced at the Dunes. Expect to see Moley and Purple fire up. Hungry will be thereabouts while Rim Job and Dolphin will be discussing their next holidays in between swings. The newbies are expected to join which will no doubt bring out the best in Pussy who needs to show some form if he`s to challenge for back to back wins.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
(8, 'Waterford Valley', '2013-11-24', 2, '2013-10-13 09:05:18', 'The second seeding event promised some improved scores from the golfing contingent and Melbourne did its best to bring out some early sunshine. Pity this didnt translate into big turnout from the group with only 3 players and 1 ring in (but what a ring in) turning up to Waterford Valley in what promised to be a friendly but fiery affair.\r\n\r\nThe day started auspiciously for the committed foursome with Purple and Dolphin smoking their drives on the first while Pussy and Rimmer found trouble on the left hand side of the first. This would be a poignant if not foreseeable day for Pussy in particular who it must be said is struggling to find the form that won him the inaugural Shankers. Rimmer recovered well and Purple started solidly in what would be one of the best days for the ring in for a long time.\r\n\r\nThe third hole (as is always the case at Waterford) saw everyone pull up short but most were happy to avoid the water on this hole. The same couldnt be said for Rimmer who decided the glory hole would be the lake on the left hand side, not once, not twice but thrice all but sinking any chance of a score on the 4th.\r\n\r\nPurple led the way with Dolphin racking up the 2s as the first half of the front 9 saw Rimmer and Pussy fill the last two positions. Dark clouds loomed over the valley as Dolphins focused waned from the repeated work phone calls about the status of a Production release interrupting his chi.\r\n\r\nHowever the day will be forever remembered for an amazing birdie off the stick from Dolphin on a power play no less. Needing to pull something out of the bag, the Dolphin drove straight down the guts on the 9th and his second was at least 30 metres to the right of the pin but on the green. Not known for his great green reads, the Dolphin measured his putt with a vicious right to left lie and duly performed the riding of the putter as he watched the ball sink into the hole. A miraculous putt which culminated in 10 Stableford points and catapulted him into the lead as the group rounded the turn.\r\n\r\nThe lofty highs soon took a familiar rollercoaster ride down for the Dolphin in an all too familiar low scoring back 9. Pussy was inconsistently consistent, Rim job plugged away courageously but the day really belonged to Purple who continued his recent rich vein of good form as he not only closed the gap on Dolphin but edged him out for top spot on the leader board.\r\n\r\nPurple finished with a magnificent score of 40, closely followed by the Dolphins 39 with Rimmer 28 and Pussy 19 rounding out the field. Its fair to say that the Purple is going to be sorely missed in April not only for his great golf play, but for the witty and jovial banter (especially towards Pussy) that weve all become accustomed too.\r\n\r\nThe next seeding event will be held at Sandringham and with the return of Hungry and the addition of the Marker, we will no doubt see some more fiery encounters as well as if anyone can catch Hungry who seems to have the tournament in the bag if the seeding events are anything to go by.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
(11, 'Sanctuary Lakes', '2014-10-19', 3, '2014-07-22 11:25:04', 'Yesterday afternoon 4 competitors braved the elements to open their accounts for the 2014/15 Shankers Seeding Tour.\r\nOn a warm and blustery day the Moth showed exactly why he is the reigning champion, picking up where he left off in Tasmania. It was a fairly solid start by all competitors with highlights being Pussy par-ing the second hole to rake in 4 stableford points - only to get way ahead of himself a few holes later and duff a straight forward chip whilst thinking of the inevitable glory coming his way and not focusing on the task at hand. Hungry Jack capitalised on the very few 2 point holes he had on the front nine, getting 3 stableford points on each. His fluid swing and consistency was on show. Moley hooked an ugly drive off the first tee, which punters feared was a sign of things to come, but he was able to recover, his mole rapers allowing him to defy the gale force winds and score on every front nine hole.\r\nAfter having to switch out carts at the turn due to a low battery only 6 points separated the field after 9 with the Moth leading on 19 and Pussy bringing up the rear on 13.\r\nThe back nine started in promising fashion for all. However, a bitter cool change with an icy wind reminiscent of Lost Farm and a non-stocked drinks cart took their toll on the intrepid foursome who all had some bad patches through the back nine. With only 9 points separating first and last at the close of play, I think all competitors will be rueing the ones that they left out there and should imbibe a steely resolve for the second Seeding event.', 'https://www.google.com/maps/embed?pb=!1m14!1m8!1m3!1d3148.4828581583106!2d144.76266099999998!3d-37.895775!3m2!1i1024!2i768!4f13.1!3m3!1m2!1s0x6ad6883f92fd9f13%3A0xf04567605305830!2sSanctuary+Lakes+Golf+Club!5e0!3m2!1sen!2sau!4v1423400536954', '12:18:00', NULL, 'http://www.sanctuarylakesclub.com.au/', '70 Greg Norman Drive SANCTUARY LAKES VIC 3030'),
(12, 'Flinders', '2014-11-16', 3, '2014-07-22 11:25:45', 'This morning the much anticipated seeding round at Flinders looked close to a wash out as the cumulus nimbus precipitated over the famed cliffs for too many consecutive hours. However as tee off arrived the skies cleared and another of mother natures forces made players earn every point scored as the wind billowed over the terrain. \r\nAfter a short and sharp session for some on the Dr Tims, singha, Shiraz and devils cut the previous night, and with Hungry Jack travelling more kilometres than any man should without a wallet, competitors met at the pro shop and awaited tee off. \r\nIt was a real tale of two groups with Moley dragging the chain in the lead (but not on the scoreboard) group unable to find any rather or tempo. The marker was hitting them cleanly but was hampered by the elements and a tour top two finishers handicap. After much discussion about handicaps Purple showed he still has some tricks up his sleeve, and although rusty after a long layoff, with the several games he`ll get under his belt prior to the tournament showed he`ll be a force to be reckoned with on and off the course up on the Sunshine Coast.\r\nGroup two came intent on capitalising on the high number of championship points available, with hungry jack looking to take out the competition literally - coming within inches of Moley with an errant tee shot. Rimmer continued his off season form being consistent from the get go and amassing 33 stable ford points on a day when anything close to 30 could be viewed as a win against the conditions. The Smoking Dolphin was affected early by the disappointment of not getting carts, but was able to claw his way back to reach second place on the day, and for the Seeding Championship.\r\nIt was a tough day for all, not only the weather but the snail like pace of the groups in front made for a challenging round. Well done to rimmer for taking the chocolates.', 'https://www.google.com/maps/embed?pb=!1m14!1m8!1m3!1d3123.442335380462!2d145.022486!3d-38.477434!3m2!1i1024!2i768!4f13.1!3m3!1m2!1s0x6ad5b8e371ffb78b%3A0xf04567605305c80!2sFlinders+Golf+Club!5e0!3m2!1sen!2sau!4v1423400579739', '12:15:00', NULL, 'http://www.flindersgolfclub.com.au/', 'Bass Street, Flinders, VIC 3929'),
(14, 'Yarra Bend', '2015-01-18', 3, '2014-08-01 12:20:06', 'Well, what a day it was for golf!\r\n\r\nFirst off, a big congratulations to Rim Job on taking out the Seeding Tour. After missing the first round he came out strong and never looked back. With the decent scores coming back to the club house at our final round at Yarra Bend, it didn`t look like Rimmer could make it a hat-trick of round wins, but doubt him at your peril. Scoring a massive 48 stableford points and 87 strokes off the stick, Rim Job left no question he is the deserved Seeding Champion and outright favourite coming into the tournament.\r\n\r\nWith healthy scores from all competitors, we saw a bit of movement on the final Seeding Championships Points Tally - the gap between second and last closing a bit. However, with three massive wins, no one had any hope of catching Rimmer.\r\n\r\nSo, how`s the form looking in the lead up to the Shankers Classic at Coolum?\r\n \r\n- Pussy Forest`s intensive summer training regime seems to be paying dividends at the right time with him recording his highest stableford score for a Shankers Round (including previous Power Play rounds). He`ll be one to watch!\r\n\r\n- The Dolphin was able to carve out a score that in any other seeding round would have seen him finish at least second. This was on only 3 hours sleep, whilst he was still having flashbacks to events at the Harry Rippers the night before. Big effort - that experience will put him in good stead to be a mover on day 2 of the tournament.\r\n\r\n- Moley slowed everything down, and whilst not setting the world on fire managed the course and his handicap to maximum reward. It`s no coincidence that on a day when the weather god`s were kind to the tour he was able to card his best score for the seeding season - if the weather is okay he can`t be discounted.\r\n\r\n- After having a questionable strategy coming into seeding and seeing his handicap creep up, the true Marker of Barnbougle 2014 began to shine through today. Similar to last year he`s got it all sussed and will be hitting his peak just as we touch down on the Sunshine coast.\r\n\r\n- When Purple came out of retirement there were nay sayers who gave him no chance of attaining his former glory. After a shaky start to the Seeding Tour the tempo is starting to come back to his game and his trademark hang time off the tee is a joy to watch. Whilst still a little underdone 7 weeks out, his form should shape up okay in time for March.\r\n\r\n- Rim Job - what more can we say? He`s been consistent since November, if his form doesn`t slip in the next 2 months it`ll take some exquisite play from someone to remove the trophy from his clutches!', 'https://www.google.com/maps/embed?pb=!1m14!1m8!1m3!1d3152.6754531856564!2d145.01208499999998!3d-37.797644999999996!3m2!1i1024!2i768!4f13.1!3m3!1m2!1s0x6ad643a352aacc39%3A0xf04567605305cf0!2sYarra+Bend+Golf+Course!5e0!3m2!1sen!2sau!4v1423400295162', '07:30:00', NULL, 'http://www.yarrabendgolf.com/', 'Yarra Bend Road Fairfield VIC 3078'),
(13, 'Waterford Valley', '2014-12-07', 3, '2014-08-01 12:19:30', 'Well, what a round! We had 7 competitors and a ring-in turn out in what can only be described as a December deluge, and we learnt several things;\r\n\r\n1. The love and passion for all things Shankers is undeniably strong, the only thing tour organisers cannot control is the weather, but we don`t let hurricanes, floods or massive fluctuation in \r\ntemperature deter us.\r\n\r\n2. After battling it out for the NAGA at the 2014 tournament, the pact that Rim Job and Dolphin made between drags of their final winnie blue before leaving the Apple Isle, to grow from that experience and contend for the major title in 2015 still drives them strongly. Both have added a consistency to their game which cannot be understated.\r\n\r\n3. Pussy Forest has turned a corner and is carving out a game style which will challenge the leaders with his high handicap. His 38 will need to drop a bit, but once we add in Power Play`s and mulligans for the big weekend this man could be unstoppable!\r\n\r\n4. The Marker is an elusive and cunning creature - did he enjoy a purple patch during the `14 tournament? Or is he taking the Seeding fixing scandal of 2013 to a whole new level? Only time will tell. The tournament steward has his eye on him!\r\n\r\n5. Moley is a fair weather golfer, if it isn`t a comfortable 22 degrees with very light winds and clear skies the slight cracks that can usually be seen in his game become gaping sink holes and canyons. If the weather up in Coolum is no good, write him off for the weekend.\r\n\r\n6. After dusting off the clubs to rejoin the tour, it`s not only Purple`s golf game that is a bit rusty, his sledging and banter needs some work too. He was 0 for 3 in getting into competitors heads today, and whilst we saw glimpses of his skill, he`ll need to put in some hard yards in the lead up to March. Luckily with the festive season upon us his off course form should be primed for the Coolum Resort... early contender for best off ground!\r\n\r\n7. As a likely non starter for the main event, Hungry Jack continues his consistent run and those eyeing off the trophy will breathe a sigh of relief not having to compete with him for the prize. He has become the first competitor in history to talk his handicap down, asking to be played off 21 from now on - there is a man comfortable in his golf shoes!\r\n\r\n8. Last but by no means least, at $17.50 the FootJoy classic glove is an absolute bargain. Available in blue, black or white it is a great stocking filler coming into Christmas!\r\n\r\nWe`ll see some handicap shuffling for the next event in an effort to ensure a tight field for Coolum in March.', 'https://www.google.com/maps/embed?pb=!1m18!1m12!1m3!1d3148.1941681942485!2d145.260651!3d-37.902523999999985!2m3!1f0!2f0!3f0!3m2!1i1024!2i768!4f13.1!3m3!1m2!1s0x6ad63da93b3c648f%3A0xf04567605305d80!2sWaterford+Valley+Golf+Course!5e0!3m2!1sen!2sau!4v1423400255974', '07:40:00', NULL, 'http://www.wvgolf.com.au/', '131 Bunjil Way Knoxfield Victoria'),
(16, 'Waterford Valley', '2015-10-11', 4, '2015-05-07 11:23:55', 'Well, what a day to open up the account for the 2015/16 Shankers Seeding Tour.\r\nThe weather gods, for the first time in 2 years at a seeding event, decided to smile on us and Waterford Valley was in top condition.\r\n\r\n<ol>\r\n<li>Teeing off from the 10th to start mixed it up a little, much to the Dolphin`s liking who amassed 7 Stableford points in his first 2 holes and 22 points on the second 9 nine!!\r\n</li><li>Purple obtained a new nickname as The Bandit as he scooped up points on all but 3 holes across the 18. It looks like the reigning NAGA`s pre-season training has paid off.\r\n</li><li>Moley took a while to get off the mark but was able to find good form, scoring 16 points in a 6 hole stretch. On the basis of today`s game you`d have to say the new irons were a wise purchase. \r\n</li><li>Marker started shakily on his comeback from successful groin relocation surgery, but with every hole the class of the man shone through a little brighter. He`ll be a force once again after he gets a bit of match fitness.\r\n<li>Hungry is... well just that. Hungry for victory! He was at the top of his game amassing 37 Stableford points for the round on a handicap of 22 - watch out!\r\n</li><li>Pussy was up to his usual tricks. Even the incentive of Tournament Points being on offer didn`t stop his penchant for strategic mind games in the seeding rounds. Lowest score for the round, but can we believe it as a true form line... I doubt it.</li>\r\n</ol>\r\nAll in all we had 5 points between 1st and 4th for Seeding Round 1, and 5 out of 6 competitors have already earned 1 bonus Tournament Point to open their account for the 2016 Road Trip by scoring 30 points.', 'https://www.google.com/maps/embed?pb=!1m18!1m12!1m3!1d6296.568684419719!2d145.26441145689083!3d-37.90041601965349!2m3!1f0!2f0!3f0!3m2!1i1024!2i768!4f13.1!3m3!1m2!1s0x6ad63da93b3c648f%3A0xf04567605305d80!2sWaterford+Valley+Golf+Course!5e0!3m2!1sen!2sau!4v1430997965404', '07:10:00', NULL, 'http://www.wvgolf.com.au/', '131 Bunjil Way Knoxfield VIC 3180'),
(17, 'Yarra Bend', '2015-11-15', 4, '2015-05-07 11:27:19', 'The second seeding event was eagerly anticipated by the Shankers contingent even though the Melbourne weather leading into the event implied that a tough day was one the cards.\r\n\r\nApart from the "roller-coaster" weather, the second seeding event was embroiled in controversy even before a ball was struck. Despite repeated confirmations that Pussy Forrest would be a willing participant, he failed to make it to the event. Even more controversial was his lack of communications to the tournaments logistics department who was patiently waiting at his door at the pre-designated time. Repeated attempts to contact Pussy were unsuccessful and the organising committee and players are genuinely concerned for his well being.\r\n\r\nAs if this wasn`t enough excitement and unwelcome distraction to the players, the Purple Headed Warrior was also absent from the day`s proceedings citing other commitments. Thankfully, through normal communications channels the SHIToC were able to confirm that Purple was indeed OK. This reporter understands that a female KY jelly wrestling competition was being held in Melbourne and lacking good judgement due to his recent diet of kale, lime beans and boiled chicken, Purple thought it a good idea to become an official sponsor of the event by donating a bunch of rakes with the catch line "Bro`s before Ho`s". \r\n\r\nNonetheless a delayed tee-off time due to these unprecedented events was inevitable and a quick re-allocation of groups saw a previously untried group of Rimmer, Hungry and Dolphin lead the way.\r\n\r\nAfter an ominous start shaking off the chilly weather and mental fatigue with all the waiting, the group performed well on the front nine with Rimmer and Hungry sharing much of the highlights. Long driving, clutch putting and bell chiming all featured, with Hungry edging out Dolphin and Rimmer, although the later was making a brave charge. Hungry was in superb touch with 3 pars on the front nine despite scratching the first.\r\n\r\nWith time against Hungry and knowing there was a risk a bonus point was at stake due to being required to make an early departure, Hungry lit up the back nine, scoring 10 points in 4 holes. Only the 14the hole brought the new favourite undone. A long iron on one of the toughest of par 3`s saw his ball end up in the bunker....from which it never got out. The same fate fell the fast finishing Rimmer and suddenly the favourites were struggling.\r\n\r\nHungry had a red hot go on the 15th and although his ball landed just off the fairway, the great man decided to pull up his tee and make his way to join Purple at the KY jelly wrestling comp. Hungry`s departure affected Rimmer badly with his first and provisional tee shots on the 15th both finding the stone quarry which resulted in a self deprecating verbal tirade towards himself.\r\n\r\nWith Dolphin there for support and a number of hits of the WADA approved NicoTin, Rimmer pulled himself together and stormed home. The most memorable being a birdie on the 17th despite the enormous pressure of crowded tee`s. \r\n\r\nThe Dolphins Movember efforts had a few punters wondering what Mitchell Johnston was doing on the Shankers tour, but he stepped up to the plate and had morale at an all time high with his on course banter. Dolphin put in a solid performance to notch up a second Pre-Tournament Bonus Point and showed consistency scoring on all but the 9th hole.  After his back 9 was notable for missed chances with 3 rim jobs almost enforcing a change of tour nickname, you can see this man isn`t far off a dominating round. It is understood the the Dolphin is considering a controversial club change in time for the next seeding event but only if he can buy it on points.\r\n\r\nMarker and Moley were joined by Shanker wannabe Ash in the second group off the tee, and after a slow start Marker showed that his pre work cheeky 9 form is no fluke. Marker`s trademark bombs off the tee became more regular as the round wore on. Never one to talk up his game, Marker was quoted in a post round interview saying he didn`t hit them all that well. A score of 21 on the back 9 (including a 14 point 5 hole streak) tells another story, seeing him win the day and proving that the recent groin relocation surgery has been a resounding success - competitors would do well to be wary of Marker coming into next years tournament. \r\n\r\nMoley dashed to the tee late after sitting outside the house of Pussy waiting for a passenger who never turned up. He was able to rally after a frenetic start and deliver 18 holes that, whilst not beautiful or conventional, kept the scoreboard ticking over. His 34 stableford points was enough to secure second place for the day, pocket a Pre-Tournament Bonus Point and have `ol Mole Raper sitting equal top the Seeding Leaderboard with Dolphin and Marker after round 2', 'https://www.google.com/maps/embed?pb=!1m18!1m12!1m3!1d3152.697901579197!2d145.011205!3d-37.797118999999995!2m3!1f0!2f0!3f0!3m2!1i1024!2i768!4f13.1!3m3!1m2!1s0x6ad643a352aacc39%3A0xf04567605305cf0!2sYarra+Bend+Golf+Course!5e0!3m2!1sen!2sau!4v1430998284922', '07:00:00', NULL, 'http://www.yarrabendgolf.com', 'Yarra Bend Road Fairfield VIC 3078'),
(18, 'Tirhatuan Lakes', '2015-12-13', 4, '2015-05-07 11:29:13', 'Well, what a success Seeding Round 3 turned out to be. The untried venue of Tirhatuan Lakes garnered almost unanimous positive feedback, and with the weather gods once again smiling on the contingent why wouldn`t it have?!\r\n\r\nWith The Marker absent due to a bout of Osteitus Pubis, we had 6 competitors vying for a win in Seeding Round 3. \r\nThe cat was set amongst the pigeons early, with a very late call from the Tournament Steward that Seeding Round 2 would be played from the yellow tees.\r\n\r\nGroup 1 consisting of Pussy, Dolphin and Hungry Jack had a mixed day.\r\nPussy took to the first tee and stated his intentions early with possibly the best tee shot of his career. He capitalised on that to rake in 4 points off the first hole, but unfortunately the hangover kicked in and he struggled the rest of the day, only able to score another 22 points on the remaining 17 holes. \r\nDolphin began with a shank off the first tee. He never really found his rhythm after that, but came home strong with a streak of 9 points on the final 4 holes to bring his tally to a respectable 29 and pick up a 3rd Pre-Tournament Bonus Point on aggregate. If he can score 29 on an average game he`s in a pretty good position coming into the new year.\r\nHungry again had another engagement to attend post round, and so asked to be in the leading group. He sped around the course, almost picking up the new nickname of `Mr Consistency` with his string of 9 two pointers on the back 9. Keep your eye on this man, he`ll be unstoppable if he ever plays a round where he`s not rushed!\r\n\r\nGroup 2 consisting of Moley, Purple and Rimmer made for intriguing viewing.\r\nWith Purple Snr. joining to make up a foursome for the day and keen to see this elite field which has relegated his first born to NAGA status our Purple Headed Warrior was nervous early. He was all over the shop, only managing to scrape together 3 points after 4 holes. But, rather than snap a club and sink beers as is his trademark, Purple gathered himself after a quick pep talk and pat on the bum from Moley to finish on 34 points and equal second for the day!\r\n\r\nMoley was up and about early bringing out the A-Grade Comedy material from the get go. His golf was not too shabby either, playing smart with good shot selection and fairly consistent execution Moley lapped up the perfect conditions to score 34 stableford points for the 3rd Seeding event in a row! Surely this is some sort of Shankers record, however this writer can`t find any relevance in it.\r\n\r\nThe day however belonged to Rimmer, in only his second seeding outing he showed why he is the reigning Shankers champ. Whilst extremely poor by his own and almost anyones standards off the tee, Rimmer showed he`s more than just a long drive. He played some exquisite recovery shots to play to his handicap of 21 and score 36 to take out the day.', 'https://www.google.com/maps/embed?pb=!1m18!1m12!1m3!1d3146.506349345787!2d145.22716185073992!3d-37.941961449063065!2m3!1f0!2f0!3f0!3m2!1i1024!2i768!4f13.1!3m3!1m2!1s0x6ad615d88d98ef21%3A0xf04567605305db0!2sTirhatuan+Lakes+Public+Golf+Course!5e0!3m2!1sen!2sau!4v1450060992451', '07:00:00', NULL, 'http://www.tirhatuangolf.com.au/', 'Corner Police & Stud Roads Rowville, Victoria, 3178'),
(19, 'Yarra Bend', '2016-01-10', 4, '2015-05-07 11:30:37', 'First and foremost, a big thanks to you the Shankers for making this years seeding tour enjoyable. The best organisation in the world counts for naught if players don`t turn up and make it fun. Seeding has been played in great spirit and was a tight competition to the end. Now that the seeds have been planted, we only have to wait 54 days for our crop to grow into the Shankers Invitational Tournament 2016 - The Road Trip!\r\n\r\nOn another beautiful day at Yarra Bend, both groups still had to be concerned with things falling from the sky, 3 near misses from other punters errant balls kept the contingent on it`s toes. With most of the group finishing within 5 points of each other for the day, handicaps are almost spot on and will only require a bit of a tweak for the Tournament weekend.\r\n\r\nAfter a marathon 12 hours on the gas, Pussy fronted up to Seeding Event 4 in all sorts of trouble, threatening to vomit throughout the entire car trip to Yarra Bend. Most competitors wrote him off for the day, but after struggling to break 20 stableford points so far this seeding tour, Pussy peeled off a brilliant 34 to show he`s still a force on the dreaded day 2 of the tournament.\r\n\r\nPurple talked a lot about Shankers Spirit for a bloke who pulled out of a seeding round at the 11th hour to watch a UFC undercard which was so C grade Foxtel didn`t even televise it. He relished in the controversy and punched out an astounding 39 points, having him second for the day, but more importantly finishing second on the Seeding Tour Ladder proving his plan of `No NAGA 2016` is well on track.\r\n\r\nAfter riding the gauntlet driving to the course after his signature go hard and go home from Dazza`s 40th the day before, Marker was in good spirits. He`d recovered well from his Osteitis Pubis and managed 34 points off a 24 handicap. He would have been much higher on the overall Seeding Ladder were it not for a missed event, he`ll be a challenger come the tournament.\r\n\r\nOur reigning tournament champion had a rollercoaster day on the course alternating good shots and bad along with good/bad holes. On a day he`d be happy to forget he still managed to finish with over 30 stableford points and claim a final Pre-Tournament bonus point. Rimmer has been in some decent form and we know he can perform on the big stage - he`s also still a motza for best beard on tour!\r\n\r\nMoley`s first tee shot rocketed into a tree and then ricocheted back 50 metres and told the story of his long game for the day. Were it not for exceptional pitching and a decent round with the putter he would have struggled to post a respectable score. This has to be a worry coming into the Tournament, a decent long game is crucial at Mission Hills and if he plays like that he can kiss any thoughts he had about getting his hands on the trophy goodbye.\r\n\r\nDolphin really had a round of 2 halves as his biggest weapon, that monster drive of his, deserted him for most of the day and 14 points at the turn had most spectators expecting a dismal back nine. But the Dolphin puffed a smoke ring out of his blow hole and charged on, getting used to the new putter and finding some driving form toward the end of the round to make a healthy 34 and equal 3rd for the day.\r\n\r\nBut the day (and Seeding Tour) belonged to Hungry, after a tyre change en route to the course he peeled off one of the most exquisite rounds this writer has seen to take honours in Shankers 2015/16 Seeding. Well done Hungry!! Surely he would be odds on favourite for the Tournament if SportsBet hadn`t suspended betting pending the outcome of the ShITOC sanctions to be handed down if Hungry does in fact miss the Magical Mystery Shankers Bus due to a wedding.\r\n\r\nLook out for your official invite to the Shankers Invitational Tournament 2016 - The Road Trip in the coming weeks which will have all the info you need for the huge weekend in March!', 'https://www.google.com/maps/embed?pb=!1m18!1m12!1m3!1d3152.697901579197!2d145.011205!3d-37.797118999999995!2m3!1f0!2f0!3f0!3m2!1i1024!2i768!4f13.1!3m3!1m2!1s0x6ad643a352aacc39%3A0xf04567605305cf0!2sYarra+Bend+Golf+Course!5e0!3m2!1sen!2sau!4v1430998284922', '07:00:00', NULL, 'http://www.yarrabendgolf.com', 'Yarra Bend Road Fairfield VIC 3078'),
(21, 'Growling Frog', '2016-08-28', 5, '2016-08-21 12:13:53', '<p class="lead">The Kluger said it was 9 degrees, but the wind chill factor made for tough conditions to kick off Shankers Seeding for the 2016/17 season. </p>\r\nWith a distinct lack of frogs, but plenty of kangaroos, our four growlers showed their commitment, with a couple of accidental rim jobs and Pussy getting very excited over Moley`s shaft!!\r\n\r\nIt was a forgettable front nine.\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>- Moley overshot five of the first 6 greens wasting some decent early play, and dropped more bombshells than this writer has had warm baths. </li>\r\n<li>- Dolphin was lucky he had his hi-viz leaders balls as he was not his usual sharp shooting self and lost one in the Australian outback due to the dangers of smoking in the bush. </li>\r\n<li>- Hungry forgot his NAGA balls, and played ok despite his new lumberjack style wood chopper swing which he has surely pulled from Trever Fairwaylover`s 1989 book "worst golf swings of the 80`s"</li>\r\n<li>- And Pussy, well he set a new course record with 72 strokes on the front nine!!</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\nThe back 9 was more impressive (closer to average than shithouse that is) as our growlers wiped their chins and went in for seconds. \r\nThe wind died down and some decent shots were witnessed every now and then, but when 4 blokes have 439 shots between them in a round of golf, the scores tell the story of the day.', 'https://www.google.com/maps/embed?pb=!1m18!1m12!1m3!1d3162.9096805132735!2d145.08576595075917!3d-37.55719167970049!2m3!1f0!2f0!3f0!3m2!1i1024!2i768!4f13.1!3m3!1m2!1s0x6ad7b4da5e8c6171%3A0xf04567605305af0!2sGrowling+Frog+Golf+Course!5e0!3m2!1sen!2sau!4v1471781668206', '07:42:00', NULL, 'growlingfroggolfcourse.com.au', '1910 Donnybrook Rd, Yan Yean VIC 3755');
INSERT INTO `seeding` (`id`, `location`, `eventdate`, `compid`, `createdate`, `writeup`, `googlemap`, `starttime`, `endtime`, `www`, `address`) VALUES
(22, 'Ringwood Golf', '2016-09-25', 5, '2016-09-06 08:56:44', 'A decidedly Smith lacking Shankers contingent turned up at Royal Ringwood and, on a brisk breezy morning, Dolphin was in no mood for discussing football after Friday nights dissapointment - this took a lot of small talk and banter right off the table from the get go.\r\n\r\nOur attention then turned to Hungry, who for the second time in a row failed to turn up with the pink NAGA balls. This saw Pussy and Moley get to work on determining the best penalty, which is sure to entail some sort of moonshine through the nostrils after playing a Power Play hole one handed.\r\n\r\nDue to the light numbers, the Shankers had to hit off in 3-2 formation with the group of Marker, Dolphin and Moley leading the charge.\r\n\r\nGroup 1 got off to a fairly uneventful front nine, but ShIT got pretty hectic on the back with a punter unhappy that Moley hadn`t called fore on the 10th. Thus began a trigger happy fore calling free for all. Dolphin and Marker decided to have a drive off, each trying to out blast the other off the tee whilst Moley marvelled at the fence megastructure lining the freeway.\r\n\r\nMarker was living up to his real name looking sharp as ever in some new specs. They proved critical too, with Marker spotting balls better than an audience member at a Thai Ladyboy show. He was in fine form golf wise, stinging them off the tee in crisp fashion. He had a solid round, and were it not for a couple of blow outs late, was a real chance of breaking 90.\r\n\r\nDolphin`s day started in undesirable fashion, when you`re three shots down and less than 100 metres from the tee on the first you have problems. But he`s the reigning champ, and regrouped by taking a splash in the water feature on the first green. He took charge, putted from the rough with aplomb and withstood a verbal barrage on the 10th to get around in a decent 98.\r\n\r\nMoley was up and down like a fiddlers elbow, playing some remarkable shots in between many shockers. It`s clear that the pressure of debuting the Apple Watch for the first time on tour got the best of him. Luckily he`s got a bit of time to work on his technology and game before making his 2018 tournament comeback.\r\n\r\nIn group 2, Pussy and Hungry were joined by two guest Shankers - Angry Steve and Mad Mitch. This should have been Pussy`s chance to shine. Clearly new to the game and with a temper that looked shorter than a skirt on King Street, Steve`s tendency to slice, miss, top and draw his big shots gave Pussy some comfort that he might not be the worst golfer on course. Mitch seemed to be a bit more consistent with the club, but by the 5th it was clear that he was in Pussy`s league when it comes to spending time in the trees.\r\n\r\nHowever, Pussy fluffed his first line, topping the ball off the 1st tee to barely trickle past the ladies start. His game continued to show few signs of improvement and on a more challenging course it`s fair to say Pussy would have been within touching distance of his record score of 156. However, some lucky reading of the greens combined with the odd half decent shot meant that Pussy`s card of 106 was somewhat more respectable than any observers might have expected.\r\n\r\nHungry however saw this as his day to shine.... accompanied by 3 below par golfers, and despite continued refusal to follow the Shankers rules he certainly took advantage of the forgiving greens and trouble free fairways. His claim of a 2.30am finish last night at drinking establishments across Melbourne is yet to be verified, but judging by the speed at which he went from 9th hole to Pie and Powerade, there seemed to be some evidence to suggest that Hungry`s was tipping back the turp`s last night. His reasoning that this was somehow connected to another failure to bring his pink balls into play were somewhat challenged by the view of ShITOC that perhaps he could have loaded up the car the day before and been somewhat more prepared.\r\n\r\nIn true Hungry style, he made a valiant attempt to negotiate his penalty for continued refusal to get his pink balls out. ShITOC are still considering whether to enforce rule 8.21.a.iv of the Shankers Rule book and insist on a "one club hole" during the competition weekend.\r\n\r\nBack to the day`s golf though - despite dissatisfaction with the speed of the greens from Hungry, along with some grumblings about the water feature on the first green, plus some dubious ball cleaning and repositioning, this was Hungry`s day. Angry Steve and Mad Mitch were inspired, impressed and in awe of the Hungry Woodchopper`s technique, distance and accuracy.', 'https://www.google.com/maps/embed?pb=!1m18!1m12!1m3!1d3151.145649169531!2d145.2216403152023!3d-37.83347597974875!2m3!1f0!2f0!3f0!3m2!1i1024!2i768!4f13.1!3m3!1m2!1s0x6ad639577324d659%3A0xf04567605305900!2sRingwood+Golf!5e0!3m2!1sen!2sau!4v1473152171622', '00:00:00', NULL, 'http://www.maroondahleisure.com.au/venues/ringwood-golf/', '352 Canterbury Road, Ringwood, VIC, 3134'),
(23, 'Sandringham', '2016-10-30', 5, '2016-11-08 09:41:11', 'On a blustery and threatening morning the Shankers returned to the mother course and birthplace of moder ShIT. For it was at Sandringham golf course where the Sharpest of Markers made his debut with a dodgy knee and a full hip flask all those years ago. \r\n\r\nThe weather gods seemed to appreciate the nostalgia, turning it on after what looked to be a long wet morning on the course. \r\n\r\n4 official handicaps, 2 hangovers and a couple of ring ins hit the course for Seeding round 3. \r\n\r\nGroup one was a Hungry Pussy Marker. Pussy rolled up after a day at the races smelling a bit like wet pub carpet. He gets an A for attitude though and, well must have been a bit pissy because he forgot to do a write up <insert Group 1 write up>\r\n\r\nGroup 2 saw a hungover Dolphin, Moley, Arsin and Allen (or Steve) tee off in front of a rambunctious gallery. \r\n\r\nDolphin was still struggling from big previous day, unsure whether he`d been on the gas for 7 or 17 hours. He was also a bit confused about which end of the club he should be holding, and a topped dribbling first tee shot in front of an expectant gallery foretold what was to come. \r\n\r\nOur reigning champion was in fine form banter wise, deliverying more jokes than a batch of Christmas crackers. Unfortunately for his golf, every second shot ended with an arched back and Dolphin looking up at the sky - evidently this makes decent progress on the golf course quite difficult. \r\n\r\nWhen Dolphins swing did resemble that of someone trying to play the game of golf his ball flight reminded us of why he`s the champ. He also managed a solid 1.89 puts per hole for the round which would have been great if he`d had at least on GIR for the day. \r\n\r\nNo amount of Gatorade was going to get him back on track, but with some solid GUI (Golfing Under the Influence) practice under his belt, a handicap that can only travel north his 1,564 point plan for a second tournament domination is right on track!\r\n\r\nMoley returned to his once favourite stomping ground and it was no surprise that he excelled especially in the tricky early morning conditions.\r\n\r\nIf the weather, course and golf wasn`t tough enough, Moley had the additional challenege of nursing a very crook Dolphin around the 10km course. This alone should have granted him another 10 stableford points.\r\n\r\nMoley started reasonably well but it wasnt until the 8th and 9 holes that Moley came into his own and left us all thankful that he wouldnt be part of the Shankers this year (he`d be joint favourite at the least). Skirting the tress on the 8th to fade the ball to the centre of the fairway, Moley then flopped an absolute gem onto the green and took the regulation to putts for his par.\r\n\r\nHe backed that up on the 9th but in more adventurous style. A good drive saw him open the hole up nicely but a duffed second left him reeling. A well flighted third left his ball precariuosly placed in between the rough, bunker and green. Facing a concrete like putting surface, Moley put the ball within an inch of the hole to nab his second par.\r\n\r\nThe back nine proved tough but motivating the Dolphin to continue was tougher not the mention the maniacal ball looking procedures that our ring ins were putting him through, it was enough to put anyone off their game.\r\n\r\nA touch over 100 for the round was an outstanding result and showed why he`s been a contender over the years.', 'https://www.google.com/maps/embed?pb=!1m18!1m12!1m3!1d3145.41617516802!2d145.02886441506132!3d-37.967415879724804!2m3!1f0!2f0!3f0!3m2!1i1024!2i768!4f13.1!3m3!1m2!1s0x6ad66a5645c08761%3A0xacc1152a1b067192!2sSandringham+Golf+Course!5e0!3m2!1sen!2sau!4v1478598046505', '08:00:00', NULL, 'http://www.sandringhamgolfcourse.com.au/', 'Cheltenham Road, Cheltenham 3192 VIC'),
(24, 'Albert Park', '2016-11-27', 5, '2016-11-29 09:29:47', 'On an overcast, but otherwise fine day 4 Shankers took on Albert Park golf course at one of the most leisurely tee times ever seen on the Seeding Tour. \r\nPussy was a notable absence, he`d got the venue wrong and was waiting for the contingent outside Sephora, unfortunately this NYC venue proved too long a commute and he wasn`t able to make the round. \r\n\r\nMarker on the other hand was jumping out of his skin to play. Turning up for a 9:45 tee off at 8:45, he was devistated to find the club house coffee machine had shat itself. Still Markers spirits were high as he looked forward to taking the packaging off his fresh new 26 handicap. He played like a 26 handicapper too, never has the tour seen so many 6`s and 7`s on a Marker scorecard. He was ok off the tee, and pretty handy with the putter, but the shots in between weren`t coming out clean at all and told the story of his day. \r\n\r\nHungry was able to learn from Markers misfortune and grab a coffee en route to the course. Sporting more modifications to his wood chopper style swing (which now incidentally has 5 distinct movements and resembles the robot dance floor move) he took to the course on with gusto. However, the consistency we have come to know and admire from the Axeman of Eltham wasn`t on show. When the new swing worked, it was awesome - but the 1 in 5 strike rate of the lumberjack style has many pundits questioning why a player of Hungry`s ability would try to change so dramatically. I understand you have to go backwards to go forwards, but it seems as though Hungry has reversed his golf game into a tree, doused it in petrol and set it on fire. One can only assume it`s some sort of tournament tactic. \r\n\r\nThe Dolphin... the reigning champion who has played more rounds at Albert Park than he`s had Winnie Blue`s, surely monstered the course. A very quick glance at his score card, what`s that? 2 birdies and 2 par`s! Very nice, surely a low 90`s round. No? So he broke 90?!?! Hang on, WTF? So he got through 4 holes in 14 strokes... and then took another 93 to get through the other 14 holes. Can`t be, can it? 67% of holes double bogey or higher. Crikey. Something is going on here, it`s already dubious that the current champ has the second highest handicap on tour, but this, well, this has me confused. The Dolphin knows Albert Park better than his dorsal fin and only had 27 puts, which means he took 80 shots to get to the green on 18 holes. He didn`t seem to chew through as many gaspers as usual, maybe nicotine is performance enhancing after all?\r\n\r\nLastly there`s Moley, who`s day can best be summed up as - meh. He didn`t set the world on fire, nor did he stink it up too pungently. Highlight of the day for Moley would have to be the exquisite drive on the 4th which went straight over the bloke in hi-viz (and his dog) and landed beautifully just near the 150m marker. Low light was his putting, this used to be a strength that has saved his bacon on numerous occasions, but over the last few rounds he`s been a combination of too long, short, left, or right - basically wherever the hole his, he doesn`t seem to putt it there. \r\n\r\nAll in all the real winner on the day was the woodsman swing action, which got a good test on the 18th with all competitors giving it a go... suffice to say I think only Hungry will be trying that one again. \r\n\r\nHere`s to the ever increasing handicaps (can`t wait to find that you`re all playing off 30+ with Pussy on the tournament weekend) and golf link wondering what they got them selves into allowing the Shankers to become official golfers.', 'https://www.google.com/maps/embed?pb=!1m18!1m12!1m3!1d3150.5157533054066!2d144.97466631505753!3d-37.8482209797462!2m3!1f0!2f0!3f0!3m2!1i1024!2i768!4f13.1!3m3!1m2!1s0x6ad6681acf2c1eed%3A0x18c3d2a861fbdbe0!2sAlbert+Park+Golf+Course!5e0!3m2!1sen!2sau!4v1480411756787', '09:45:00', NULL, 'https://www.albertparkgolf.com.au/', 'Queens Rd & Lakeside Dr, Melbourne VIC 3004'),
(25, 'Sandhurst Champions Course', '2016-12-11', 5, '2016-12-14 09:58:23', 'Two current Shankers, the 2015 Shankers Champ and guest Irishman lined up for the first official attendance by Shankers at a proper, grown up competition.  The Social Golf Club Christmas event at Sandhurst was the venue for what would turn out to be a day to remember in Shankers History.\r\n\r\nThe Marker`s handicap for the day was a tasty 30 and with Pussy`s realisation that his 36 handicap left no room for any additional help from the slope rating, he was going to need to pull out the big shots to stand a chance of putting in a respectable score for the day.\r\n\r\nAfter weeks of baby induced sleep deprivation on the back of some dubious medical and physical examinations from the boys in blue,  Rimmer was somewhat low in confidence as the group tee`d off from the 12th in a shotgun start.  Fortunately, our guest golfer Leetchy set a low bar off the tee and despite a few rusty shots, Rimmer reminded us why he won the 2015 comp and then went on to destroy the rest of the field in the 2016 seeding events.\r\n\r\nIt wasn`t long before the Marker showed us why he`s a crowd favourite to take out the 2017 tournament. Sleep deprivation was more recent for the Sharp One as he stepped up to the comp with just 3 hours of shut-eye, but he didn`t let this affect his commitment to the game.  With a consistent swing and technique that Nick Faldo would be proud of, it`s a mystery why the Marker is yet to be crowned champ. Teeing off from the 16th par 3, the Marker landed the ball within a short man`s club`s length of the hole and chalked himself up on the the first of the comp`s three Nearest the Pin boards.\r\n\r\nPussy meanwhile was making the most of his 2 extra shots per hole, and confounding the experts was yet again raising his game under the pressure of the comp.  While scratching a hole here and there, he made the most of the holes he did complete and by the end of the first 9 was traveling well on a handicap matching 18 stableford points.\r\n\r\nThe Marker continued to blow hot and cold - not content with nearest the pin, he was within a bee`s dick of the longest drive.  And but for the unfortunate drive by at that moment of the tournament organisers, it could arguably have been blown a couple of mm forward by a gust of wind to chalk up Marker on the second of two comp boards.  \r\n\r\nLeetchy played the comedy shot of the day out of 6 inches of water, followed by a recovery shot out the love grass from behind a tree that nearly plopped in the hole... Pussy came as close as he ever will to chipping in, and Rimmer started tonking the ball as we know he can in order to minimise shots and maximise time to puff on the camberwell carrot.\r\n\r\nOne more surprise for the day saw Leetchy recover from a round that even Pussy would have considered average, to land the ball closest to the pin on the 8th and knock Biker Ken off the tally.  \r\n\r\nAll 4 players finished up with close, but not quite, candidates for nearest the pin on the final 11th hole to end an enjoyable, yet hardly career changing round.\r\n\r\nWith 2 nearest the pin candidates, the Shankers were like a little ball of excitable excitement going into the presentations.  Tucking into the 2nd sausage sizzle and first beer of the day, the announcement of the 3rd place overall winner on 37 points hardly registered with Pussy and Marker... until The Social Golf club announced "in 3rd place, Julian Stevenson"!  Wow, what a day for the Shankers Champ who never was... just 2 stableford points away from taking out the comp, a couple of loose puts was all that stood between Pussy and the glory hole.\r\n\r\nAfter 1st and 2nd place were announced, next up "Nearest the pin on the 16th is Paul Sharp".  Boom!  The Marker gleefully accepted his spanking new glove and balls.\r\n\r\nJust to end the day on a high, our guest golfer Leetchy was then announced as the winner of the Nearest the Pin on the 8th! Boom, boom!  A hatrick of awards for the group.  \r\n\r\nA successful first foray into the world of grown up competition golf for the Shankers.\r\n\r\nFootnote:  Pussy`s glory was short lived, following his somewhat harsh treatment following the competition, as Golflink dropped his handicap down to a completely unreasonable 29.', 'https://www.google.com/maps/embed?pb=!1m18!1m12!1m3!1d3140.6384447065466!2d145.208369515065!3d-38.07880047970536!2m3!1f0!2f0!3f0!3m2!1i1024!2i768!4f13.1!3m3!1m2!1s0x6ad60dc1bbbc74ed%3A0x19eb8b40259c9b28!2sSandhurst+Club!5e0!3m2!1sen!2sau!4v1481709430735', '07:30:00', NULL, 'https://www.sandhurst.com/golf-courses/', '75 Sandhurst Blvd, Sandhurst'),
(26, 'Yarra Bend', '2017-01-22', 5, '2017-03-22 10:53:50', 'On a typically f&*king stinking hot one in Melbourne, 4 Shankers took on a Yarra Bend course in mint condition at a very un-Shankers time slot.\r\n \r\nPussy had only finished drinking 10.5 hours earlier, which is no mean feat when you have a 2pm tee off. He grumbled his way to the first tee and connected better than this writer has seen him do in a long time  no wonder Golf Australia has lowered his handicap! But Pussy seemed to be playing less like Aaron Baddeley and more like Hanse Cronje, as the seemed to throw the first couple of holes. Im not sure whether this was due to taking money from book makers, or a desire to get himself back up above the Dolphins 31 Handicap. After a few comments from the other Shankers he did pick up his game, and displayed some of the golf that saw his handicap plummet 7 shots in a single round. Hes playing full of confidence, never more evident than on the 9th where he was in two minds whether to wait for the group in front to leave the green when taking his second shot 243 metres from the pin.\r\n \r\nThe Dolphin was full of beans like Warnies carry-on bag prior to a tour of India. Im not sure whether he was more excited about a post noon tee off or his 31 Handicap. The banter started early, and he seemed to be the only 2017 contender actually trying on the first few holes. Dolphin sorted that out over the next couple though, playing a game of how many times can I over shoot the green on the short 4th Par 3. All in all it was a step in the right direction for our newly crowned 31 Handicapper, he managed a birdie late in the piece and a few pars along the way to post his best round of 2017 seeding to date. He`s on the right track coming into the tournament.\r\n \r\nMarker fronted up looking very sharp as usual, at first glance you couldnt tell the man had endured an 11 hour bender the day before and an 8am breakfast. His golf told the story though, his first few holes went something like 8,7,6 but Im not sure the trend downward continued as planned. He showed flashes of his brilliance, particularly off the tee, enough to put to rest those rumours of a third groin relocation surgery. Hes put in the right type of training, turning up to seeding events hungover time and time again. This will hold him in good stead for the big rAdelaide weekend and with his 26 handicap I have to agree with an early call from the Dolphin  if you see an engraving shop with 20% just put the Marker down now.\r\n \r\nMoley was out before he even got to the course, sitting at home with a fatigued 8+ month pregnant defacto, a rambunctious 4 year old and a glistening pool, his head was never in the game. Its hard to motivate yourself for a Seeding Round when you wont be taking part in the ultimate event. He struck the ball cleanly, and showed enough to say he probably would be a contender on the weekend. There were a couple of displays of nonchalant 4 putting, and a 9th hole exit which told his mind was else where. Moley has 13 months to prepare his assault on the 2018 championship  and training starts now. Well maybe in a few months once hes not elbow deep in nappies.\r\n \r\nThanks for the balls fellas, appreciate the gesture. Good luck for the big weekend, and remember what old mate Trever Fairwalover always says  the reason a golf pro tells you to keep your head down is so that you dont see him laughing.', 'https://www.google.com/maps/embed?pb=!1m18!1m12!1m3!1d3152.6482424848286!2d145.01385261531834!3d-37.798282579755124!2m3!1f0!2f0!3f0!3m2!1i1024!2i768!4f13.1!3m3!1m2!1s0x6ad643a352aacc39%3A0xf04567605305cf0!2sYarra+Bend+Golf!5e0!3m2!1sen!2sau!4v1490180096289', '02:00:00', NULL, 'www.yarrabendgolf.com', 'Yarra Bend Road, Fairfield'),
(27, 'Sandringham', '2017-10-08', 6, '2017-09-25 04:40:04', 'On a Spring day with the wind howling like a Banshee in mating season, 4 Shankers turned up at the hallowed turf of Sandringham Golf course smiling from ear to ear as the kicked off another seeding season.\r\n\r\nDolphins WhatsApp silence had been deafening in the lead up to the round, and its still unclear as to whether is Huawei p370 running the FkN-P0v operating system allows him to receive messages or email. Surely not, as the only logical explanation for his wayward golf would be tanking, which we all know will cost him bonus points under the new seeding rules. The great banter weve come to expect from the Dolph was on display, however except for a few holes reminiscent of his 2016 form, he looked like a golfer who has spent the winter enjoying his footy. Hell be better for the run though, and well expect big improvement as we near the pointy end of the tour. \r\n\r\nPussy has a love/hate relationship with pink. He was caressing his pink balls better than a well paid hooker. His drives were crisp, he pitched better than Randy Johnson, and wasnt too shabby with the putter either. He clearly is on a mission to not be NAGA for long, and playing off a sub 30 handicap for the first time in tour history, he showed that he will be a farce (sic) to be reckoned with come the tournament weekend.... then we hit the back 9. His 48 putt effort on the 11th showed us hes a deserving NAGA, he showed signs of fading as the round wore on. Consistency over 18 holes should be his goal during seeding. \r\n\r\nPlaying less like the 2017 champion and more like the 2016 NAGA, you could have been forgiven for thinking Hungry had bought his yellow hat from a $7 discount bin rather than earned it by winning the tournament. His golf was erratic but somehow seemed to improve when the idea of negative bonus points for increasing your handicap during Seeding was floated. Hes a proud man, and became Hangry several times, most notably throwing a club in rage after a wayward shot on the 12th. Hangry plays an agressive style of golf, real risk vs. reward stuff, and the risks were much greater with hurricane Irene bearing down on the group. Its early days, and we know this man will find form when it counts. \r\n\r\nAfter 8 months in the wilderness, Moley made an emphatic return to Shankers competition golf.  His lazy swing could be mistaken for nonchalance, but it was clear that just below the surface of that relaxed swing was a man determined to be the 6th name on the ShIT trophy in 2018.  Like a homecoming queen, he almost made Sandringham Links his own - although his clever tactic of paying people to hide in bushes to find his wayward balls almost backfired when he fired his ball into the ladies tee-bushes on the 11th... after 8 seconds of suspense-filled silence, his "that balls not coming out" call was enough to remind his hidden helper to chuck the ball back into play. Moley continued hit some sweet shots off the tee, but his putting got in the way of him playing anything resembling decent golf or getting closer to a bonus point.', 'https://www.google.com/maps/embed?pb=!1m18!1m12!1m3!1d3145.41617516802!2d145.02886441506132!3d-37.967415879724804!2m3!1f0!2f0!3f0!3m2!1i1024!2i768!4f13.1!3m3!1m2!1s0x6ad66a5645c08761%3A0xacc1152a1b067192!2sSandringham+Golf+Course!5e0!3m2!1sen!2sau!4v1478598046505', '08:37:00', NULL, 'http://www.sandringhamgolfcourse.com.au/', 'Cheltenham Road, Cheltenham 3192 VIC'),
(28, 'Kingston Links', '2017-11-12', 6, '2017-11-12 11:17:50', 'On a day that forecast a beautiful 27 degrees, the Shankers contingent headed to Kingston Links in shorts and with ample sunscreen to protect them from the elements. Alas, the closer they got to Rowville the thicker the fog became and the team ended up teeing off in hazy, overcast and drizzly conditions to the sound of the dull hum from the overhead power lines. \r\n\r\nGroup 1 saw some less than magnificent first hole drives from Marker, Hungry, Dolphin and Moley as the contingent kicked off Seeding Round 2 in less than ideal fashion.  Pussy was the only official Shanker in group 2 as he was joined by regular guest Shanker, Irish "The Bloodsucker" Andrew and Emile the Gunner.\r\n\r\nHungry had a solid day on the course, with the hangry temper tantrums of Sandringham a distant memory. He played sublime approach shots, his putting was on song and some of his drives caused concern for air traffic control with their massive trajectory. However, with the good comes the bad and Hungry saw some trouble with sand traps and bunkers - one low light was 2 shots in a sand trap, only for the second to land in the drink and scratch the hole. As the round drew to a close Hungry lost his fluidity, ShITOC will be reviewing the tapes to ensure he isn`t tanking in preparation for an assault on the double title.\r\n\r\nMarker (AKA Frenchie) took to the fairways for what was the first time since the 2017 tournament if the Adelaide tags on his golf bag were anything to go by. Exactly how much Marker had to bribe Golf Australia to be handed such a generous handicap of 25 is unknown, but it must have been a handsome sum. Not sure it`ll stay so high for too much longer after he dominated Kingston Links to plunder a ridiculous 45 stableford points. All facets of his game were in fine form, hopefully he hasn`t peaked too early and can take this kind of game into the 2018 tournament and finally hold aloft the trophy. Sportsbet has him an early short favourite. \r\n\r\nAfter several days of bachelorhood, and fresh from evading nasty penalties by finally submitting his Seeding Round 1 scorecard, Dolphin hit the course with gusto. His full banter prowess was on display whereas his golf was a bit hit and miss. He didn`t have any good holes... just great ones and ones that youd wipe twice after a fiery curry. He can be forgiven for his erratic performance given he detoured via Bendigo to get to the course after encountering several road closures. An average end result with only 27 points for the round has the golfing world wondering if Dolphin is trying to take the title of "highest Shankers handicap" off Pussy Forest. \r\n\r\nMoley is back!! Just to clarify - back in that hes hitting them off the tee lower than ever. And as if he felt he hadnt burnt enough worms with his drives, he was also bulldozing earth worms on the greens too. Hes a slow learner is our man Moley - taking 8 holes to realise that the rooster tail of water following his ball on each putt meant that the greens were slow. There`s always one part of his game thats in decent order though, and today that was his approach shots. Laser like precision saved his game, but hell need to curtail the back 9 fade outs if hes a chance at the 2018 tournament. \r\n\r\nAfter finally unwrapping his driver after 4 long years of unnecessarily cluttering his golf bag, Pussy made the most of the extra 2.5 metres he now gets off the tee and managed a very respectable (by his below-mediocre standards) 15 stableford points on the front 9.  Undistracted by the frequent plop of balls in water (reminding Pussy of that time in Thailand with the ladyboy and the hot tub) from Emile`s ever diminishing supply of golf balls, Pussy showed consistency on the front 9 that has so often been his nemesis.  Straight tee-shots and steady putting left only the shots in between to get in the way of a first half performance that promised much and delivered mediocrity.  Pussy`s back nine though was something that pundits will ponder over for many seconds... 2 pars, 2 holes with a single putt and just one hole with a 3 putt should have left Pussy with his best score since that minger in Middlesborough in the 80`s.  But add in the 12 shots out the sand across 4 holes it becomes clear why Pussy yet again failed to show anything in the way of improvement since he first picked up a club in 1989.  Ending the day on 30 stableford points left Pussy pondering how he will deal with the new NAGA rules during the 2018 Shankers weekend.', 'https://www.google.com/maps/embed?pb=!1m18!1m12!1m3!1d3147.4643502323224!2d145.21673031531455!3d-37.919581147878844!2m3!1f0!2f0!3f0!3m2!1i1024!2i768!4f13.1!3m3!1m2!1s0x6ad615fb94746801%3A0xf4f3a3ea5373431d!2sKingston+Links+Golf+Club!5e0!3m2!1sen!2sau!4v1510485444372', '07:04:00', NULL, 'http://www.kingstonlinks.com.au/', '14 Corporate Avenue Rowville'),
(29, 'Yarra Bend', '2017-12-10', 6, '2018-01-22 05:13:32', '', 'https://www.google.com/maps/embed?pb=!1m14!1m8!1m3!1d12610.789796798981!2d145.0113206!3d-37.7971296!3m2!1i1024!2i768!4f13.1!3m3!1m2!1s0x0%3A0xf04567605305cf0!2sYarra+Bend+Golf!5e0!3m2!1sen!2sau!4v1516597952235', '08:37:00', NULL, 'http://www.yarrabendgolf.com/', 'Fairfield, VIC'),
(30, 'Growling Frog', '2018-01-22', 6, '2018-01-22 05:14:57', 'A strong Shankers contingent made the very early morning drive through the winding roads out to Yan Yean with a sense of excitement and trepidation. Excited that with the closing of 2018 Seeding the tournament is less than 50 days away, but nervous as to what the Growling Frog would serve up. Almost 15 months since the first ShITOC foray onto the most challenging course the Nillumbik Shire has to offer, the Shankers rightly feel that their golfing prowess has improved... Would the results of the day confirm that? Or, would the Growl teach the Shankers another golfing lesson causing untold psychological damage leading into the tournament?\r\n\r\n5 hours after teeing off we had the answer, in a win for ShITOC the frogs growl turned to a half hearted ribbit. All Shankers scored 30+ stableford points and a measly 8 points separating 1st from last. It shows we`re in for a crakcking tournament this year where well used Power Plays could be the difference between glory and despair.\r\n\r\n\r\nThe first group were the Shankers A-Listers - consisting of recently anointed Shanker, Ash "The farrier" McKnight who plays of single figures, Reigning 2018 Champion Hungry Jack and Dolph (the 2017 champ) to lead us off on the first.\r\n\r\nWith this being the official last seeding round, the first group were keen to make big in roads into their scoring and the Farrier lead the charge with some long and strong hitting. He was the picture of consistency on the front 9 and Doz and Dolph could only watch in amazement.\r\n\r\nFarrier`s banter was also worth noting with sage advice (legitimate) for Doz and Dolph to assit their game and some genuine sledging directed to Hungry around his wayward tee shots. It brought back memories of the great Purple and if this level of banter was anything to go by, Farrier will fit in nicely on the tour.\r\n\r\nHungry had an inconsistent front 9 with wayward drives of the tee not helping his cause. However with the typical grit we`ve come to expect from Hungry, his recovery shots to the green were a sight to behold. Although Rimmer wasn`t part of our group, Hungry certainly channeled him in spirit, leaving close to 6 shots on the green with some of the finest rim jobs and hole tickles, that even Peter North would have been proud off.\r\n\r\nDolph, ironically had a very consistent front 9 with nothing memorable or notable to write home about. Scoring every hole even with the zig-zagging nature of his shots (walking an extra kilometer than Hungry and Farrier). Finishing on a respectable 19 points for the first 9, one can only garner that the 32 handicap plus the elevated performance of Farrier lifted his game.\r\n\r\nThe back 9 saw a resurgence of Hungry as with a good coffee and Pete`s unhygienic brekky roll, Hungry started to show the kind of golf that won him the tournament. Tee shots improved and some very solid putting, including a birdie saw him build in confidence to the point where he was even instigating conversation with Farrier and Dolph.\r\n\r\nFor Farrier, the back 9 unearthed some chinks in the armour. He famously predicted a birdie on the 11th and proceeded to duff the first 3 shots but still managed to scrape in a point. Power Plays and some pressure build up to try and play to par can certainly unnerve the horse whisperer and Shankers should take any and all opportunities to do so. Needing 4 points on the last hole to play to par, Farrier smoked his drive to land around 88 meters from the flag. A birdie would give him the 4 points but his second shot landed a good 10 meters from the hole. He came within a public hair on a 70`s porn star from having it drop but finished with a respectable par on one of the toughest holes on the course.\r\n\r\nDolph again had a consistent but not memorable back 9 managing a lone par for the day. However amassing 2 and 3 points over 8 of the 9 holes saw him finishing with 20 points on the back 9. Landing on 39 for the day equal with Pussy, Dolph has certainly done himself no favours as a lower handicap and his infamous inconsistency especially on tour will see him making up the numbers rather than challenging. Expect to see him play a good hand in the sledging on tour.\r\n\r\nThe 2nd group off the tee saw a motley crew. Rimmer made a much anticipated guest appearance, along with the Tour President and Tournament Steward. Rounding out the foursome was another guest Adam - aka Moth 2. With 4 fairly decent tee shots off the first, the group embarked on their round in very high spirits.\r\n\r\nPussy Forest the man who has embraced being NAGA like no other in tour history had a blistering round with a massive swag of 39 points. With the slope rating bumping him up to a 36 handicap, he made the most of his 2 shots on each hole. Having spent the off season reconstructing his famous pre shot bum wiggle, the hours spent in twerk training really paid dividends. The pink capped cat was extremely consistent off the tee, and whilst his putting didn`t trouble the editors of the highlight reel he was extremely solid on the green and didn`t leave much out there. The sand was his only Achilles heel for the day, taking multiple shots in 3 or 4 bunkers one can only imagine the heights he may have reached had this not been the case. Pussy is on top of his game, and his love affair with the pink balls and cap looks to be over.\r\n\r\nMoley came to the course in a positive mindset hoping to convert his recent astonishing digital form on an iPhone golf game to the real world. He soon found that there was absolutely no correlation to his in app and on course performance, and with Pussy ticking the score over nicely Moley had to re-adjust quick! And that he did, his 3rd hole birdie dance celebration rivalled that of the most organised flash mob. Amassing 19 points on the front nine with 2 scratchings to his name, the glucose from the brekky burger seemed to cause him issues and  we saw a very very slow start on the back. Some mammoth putts and well executed flop shots helped him recover to produce a tidy score without setting the world on fire. The next 6 weeks of prep will be important to his tournament chances.\r\n\r\nRimmer made his return to Shankers looking more relaxed than stock broker after a happy ending massage. With no expectations, and no score card in sight we saw glimpses of the form that had this man holding the 2016 trophy high. For a bloke who couldn`t remember the last time he played, there was enough quality on show to demonstrate that it would only take a few rounds to be a challenger again... who knows, maybe we`ll see him make a 2019 comeback???\r\n\r\nAdam (or Alan as Dolph called him upon introduction) "The Bandit/Moth 2" showed his devious hand very early. After talking up the fact he only plays "once very 12 months" and would "probably be off 30" he proceeded to blast a huge drive off the first tee and drop his 2nd approach shot duly on the dance floor. The banter was loud and proud, and although he did hit a few wayward shots here and there, there was a definite length and consistency to his game that showed a 30 handicap would see this bloke averaging around 48 stableford points a round.\r\n\r\nAll in all a great way to kick off the year, and a cracking end to a sensational Seeding Tour.', 'https://www.google.com/maps/embed?pb=!1m14!1m8!1m3!1d12651.40449509739!2d145.0885291!3d-37.5585712!3m2!1i1024!2i768!4f13.1!3m3!1m2!1s0x0%3A0xf04567605305af0!2sGrowling+Frog+Golf+Course!5e0!3m2!1sen!2sau!4v1516598045675', '07:10:00', NULL, 'growlingfroggolfcourse.com.au', '1910 Donnybrook Rd, Yan Yean VIC'),
